{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"floaty-precious-rodent","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\n\nEven with schema-filtered selection (the selection story this depends on), extraction from\nfree text stays heuristic: a trailing schema-valid decoy can win, and models fence-wrap quoted\nJSON so fences cannot serve as the channel (measured: E2 catch 2, experiment-results comment\non the selection bug). An explicit output channel makes the payload location a stated contract\ninstead of an inference.\n\n## Approach\n\nExtend `schema_directive` (src/rebar/llm/structured.py:63) to instruct the model to wrap its\nsingle final JSON object between the literal markers `<<<REBAR_OUTPUT>>>` and `<<<END>>>`.\nExtraction in `parse_structured` (:212) tries marker-delimited blocks FIRST — the LAST marker\nblock wins, validated via `validate_to` (:177) — and falls back to the selection pipeline for\nmarkerless replies, so older transcripts and non-compliant models degrade gracefully.\n\nDirective and extraction land in ONE change, deliberately: E2 measured that shipping the\ndirective alone flips quote-in-prose from 0% to 100% and breaks the current parser 10/10 — a\nsplit would leave the system broken between changes. The marker literal is the E2-tested one\n(16/16 compliance across sonnet/haiku on Bedrock, 0/26 decoy wins). Prior art: Anthropic's\nanswer-tag extraction guidance and aider's `<<<`-style sentinel blocks; markdown fences are\ndisqualified as the channel because models fence-wrap quoted material (E2). The directive is\nappended to the user prompt at src/rebar/llm/structured_run.py:202 (`schema_hint`), which is\ncache-prefix-neutral; that call site does not change.\n\n## Scope\n\n- src/rebar/llm/structured.py — directive text + marker extraction in `parse_structured`\n- tests/unit/test_structured.py — marker pins, incl. the fenced-quote hazard pin\n- tests/fixtures/ — E2 sentinel replies added to the corpus\n\n## Testing\n\nUnit/contract tier (real reply text through the real parser):\n\n- Marker extraction pins: one block; multiple blocks -> LAST wins; markerless -> selection\n  fallback yields the identical result (parameterized contrast against the selection story's\n  tests); marker block containing a fenced object -> payload still wins.\n- The fenced-quote hazard pin: a fence-wrapped schema-decoy plus a marker-wrapped payload ->\n  the marker payload wins (regression pin for E2 catch 2).\n- Mutation check: dropping marker priority (extraction ignores markers) turns the E2-reply\n  corpus test RED.\n- LLM-surface evidence is measured by the harness story (test-design §10: paired directives,\n  fixed n, deterministic scoring) and recorded here as an operator-attested artifact.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The directive names both markers and extraction honors them with last-block-wins —\n      checked by the new unit pins in tests/unit/test_structured.py.\n- [ ] A markerless reply falls back to schema-filtered selection with identical results —\n      checked by a parameterized contrast test.\n- [ ] A fence-wrapped decoy alongside a marker-wrapped payload parses to the payload — checked\n      by the pinned hazard test.\n- [ ] [operator-attested] A harness before/after run (old vs sentinel directive) shows parse\n      success at or above the predeclared threshold (>= 95% per cell) with the artifact link\n      recorded as a comment on this ticket.","id":"4ca2-97b4-51fb-41c9","parent_id":"196d-28c4-ef0f-445c","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Sentinel output channel for prompted structured replies"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785891859688051001,"uuid":"aee0f540-cbbc-4f47-913d-366859c36d2f"}